WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
This is the last Module 8 video, and

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.840
it's practice.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.640
Evaluate questions in this module ask you to

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.360
judge a prevention method or a technology, using

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.640
evidence.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.960
Here are three HSC-style questions: a screening campaign,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.320
a gene therapy and a hearing technology.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.120
Pause and try each one properly, then we'll

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.240
work through it together.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:24.546
Question one.

00:00:24.827 --> 00:00:27.226
A state ran a two-year campaign to get

00:00:27.307 --> 00:00:30.506
more people aged fifty to seventy-four to return

00:00:30.587 --> 00:00:33.066
their free bowel cancer screening kits.

00:00:33.387 --> 00:00:36.106
Region A received the campaign, with letters from

00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:38.186
local doctors and text reminders.

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:41.786
Region B, similar in age and income, received

00:00:41.827 --> 00:00:43.106
the kits only.

00:00:43.387 --> 00:00:45.706
The table shows the percentage of kits returned

00:00:45.987 --> 00:00:47.346
before and after.

00:00:47.627 --> 00:00:50.386
Evaluate the effectiveness of the campaign, using the

00:00:50.427 --> 00:00:50.906
data.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.906
Pause here to answer.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.933
Start with how screening prevents harm.

00:01:06.214 --> 00:01:08.693
The kit finds hidden blood, and a positive

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:11.093
result leads to a closer look inside the

00:01:11.174 --> 00:01:14.213
bowel, where growths called polyps can be removed

00:01:14.294 --> 00:01:17.333
before they become cancer, or a cancer found

00:01:17.414 --> 00:01:18.133
early.

00:01:18.454 --> 00:01:21.093
So returning a kit is an impact measure:

00:01:21.174 --> 00:01:23.733
what people did, not yet what the disease

00:01:23.814 --> 00:01:24.053
did.

00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:26.333
Now use the comparison.

00:01:26.614 --> 00:01:29.493
Region A rose by nine percentage points, and

00:01:29.574 --> 00:01:32.613
Region B, without the campaign, rose by two.

00:01:33.094 --> 00:01:35.253
So about seven points can be linked to

00:01:35.334 --> 00:01:36.213
the campaign.

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:38.833
Now the limits.

00:01:39.114 --> 00:01:42.393
These data measure kit returns, not deaths, and

00:01:42.514 --> 00:01:44.793
longer follow-up would test health outcomes.

00:01:45.354 --> 00:01:47.993
The regions weren't chosen at random, so other

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:49.273
differences might matter.

00:01:49.754 --> 00:01:52.153
And more than half of Region A still

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.633
didn't return a kit.

00:01:53.994 --> 00:01:57.113
So the campaign was effective at increasing screening,

00:01:57.194 --> 00:01:59.833
which is promising for preventing deaths, but that

00:02:00.034 --> 00:02:01.273
outcome isn't shown yet.

00:02:01.914 --> 00:02:05.353
A good improvement: follow early diagnoses and deaths

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.593
for ten years or more, and target the

00:02:07.674 --> 00:02:09.993
groups least likely to return kits.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.840
The classic mistake is saying the campaign raised

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.080
returns by nine points.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:19.040
Region B rose by two without it, perhaps

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.760
from news stories or wider awareness.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.640
The comparison region is what separates the campaign's

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.520
effect from everything else that changed.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.320
Compare with it before you credit the campaign.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.413
Question two.

00:02:32.974 --> 00:02:35.693
An inherited eye disease is caused by two

00:02:35.774 --> 00:02:39.933
faulty copies of a gene called RPE65.

00:02:40.094 --> 00:02:42.973
Without its protein, the retina can't keep remaking

00:02:43.054 --> 00:02:46.333
the pigment that detects light, so vision worsens,

00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:48.653
and many people become blind.

00:02:48.694 --> 00:02:51.453
In a trial, a harmless virus carried working

00:02:51.614 --> 00:02:53.533
copies of the gene into the retinas of

00:02:53.694 --> 00:02:54.733
twenty people.

00:02:54.814 --> 00:02:56.653
Ten others were not treated.

00:02:56.814 --> 00:02:59.853
After a year, thirteen treated people, and none

00:02:59.894 --> 00:03:02.013
of the untreated, could find their way through

00:03:02.094 --> 00:03:04.413
a test course in the dimmest light.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.733
Explain how this therapy works.

00:03:06.894 --> 00:03:08.973
Then evaluate it as a way to prevent

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.253
vision loss.

00:03:10.414 --> 00:03:11.613
Pause here to answer.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.433
Explain first.

00:03:23.714 --> 00:03:26.673
The virus is a vector: it delivers working

00:03:26.754 --> 00:03:29.393
copies of the gene into retinal cells, and

00:03:29.474 --> 00:03:31.473
those cells use them to make the missing

00:03:31.554 --> 00:03:34.033
protein, so the retina can respond to light

00:03:34.114 --> 00:03:34.433
again.

00:03:35.154 --> 00:03:37.073
Now ask what this prevents.

00:03:37.554 --> 00:03:39.713
It aims to prevent further vision loss in

00:03:39.794 --> 00:03:42.593
the treated person, a change to the phenotype.

00:03:43.074 --> 00:03:45.313
It doesn't change their eggs or sperm, so

00:03:45.394 --> 00:03:47.873
their children can still inherit the faulty gene.

00:03:48.354 --> 00:03:50.433
And it can only rescue retinal cells that

00:03:50.514 --> 00:03:51.633
are still alive.

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:53.793
Now the data.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:57.633
Thirteen of twenty is sixty-five per cent, against

00:03:57.794 --> 00:04:00.913
none of ten, and the untreated group strengthens

00:04:00.954 --> 00:04:03.953
the evidence that treatment caused the improvement.

00:04:04.114 --> 00:04:06.433
But it's a small trial, followed for one

00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:08.993
year, and it helps only people with this

00:04:09.074 --> 00:04:11.793
one gene fault, a small share of inherited

00:04:11.874 --> 00:04:12.913
blindness.

00:04:12.994 --> 00:04:15.233
It's very expensive, too.

00:04:15.394 --> 00:04:18.113
So it improved functional vision over one year

00:04:18.194 --> 00:04:20.593
for this gene fault, but the trial doesn't

00:04:20.674 --> 00:04:22.913
show the retina has stopped declining.

00:04:22.994 --> 00:04:25.393
It can't prevent inherited eye disease across a

00:04:25.474 --> 00:04:26.353
population.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.126
The classic mistake is writing that this gene

00:04:30.207 --> 00:04:32.966
therapy stops the disease being passed on.

00:04:33.247 --> 00:04:36.126
It changes body cells in one person.

00:04:36.247 --> 00:04:38.526
Their eggs or sperm still carry the faulty

00:04:38.607 --> 00:04:40.926
gene, so the risk for their children is

00:04:41.007 --> 00:04:41.886
unchanged.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.060
Question three.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.340
A clinic fits cochlear implants for adults with

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.700
severe to profound hearing loss.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:53.420
Its report says, "Our program is a success:

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:55.980
we fitted thirty implants this year, up from

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:56.700
eighteen."

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.660
The table shows speech test results for those

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.940
thirty adults, with their best hearing aids before,

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.180
and twelve months after the implant.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.020
Explain why the number fitted doesn't measure effectiveness,

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.620
and identify a better outcome measure.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.100
Then evaluate the implants, using the data and

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:16.620
one access issue.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:18.220
Pause here to answer.

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:31.353
Thirty implants fitted is a process measure.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:34.073
It counts what the clinic did, not what

00:05:34.154 --> 00:05:35.793
changed for the patients.

00:05:36.154 --> 00:05:39.673
The disorder's effect is trouble understanding speech, so

00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:42.073
the meaningful outcome is the speech score.

00:05:42.634 --> 00:05:44.873
It rose from fifteen to seventy per cent

00:05:44.954 --> 00:05:47.833
in quiet, and from five to thirty-five in

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:48.473
noise.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:51.593
Comparing each person with their own best hearing

00:05:51.674 --> 00:05:54.393
aids is a fair baseline, and twenty-eight of

00:05:54.474 --> 00:05:57.113
thirty still use the implant every day.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.373
Now the limits.

00:05:59.654 --> 00:06:03.213
Noise is still hard: thirty-five per cent means

00:06:03.374 --> 00:06:04.573
most words are missed.

00:06:05.054 --> 00:06:07.613
It's one clinic, with no comparison group.

00:06:08.094 --> 00:06:10.653
And for access, the average wait is nine

00:06:10.814 --> 00:06:14.173
months, and an implant needs surgery, programming and

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:17.133
months of practice, which not everyone can reach.

00:06:17.774 --> 00:06:20.013
So the implants are highly effective at giving

00:06:20.094 --> 00:06:22.893
these adults access to speech in quiet, and

00:06:22.974 --> 00:06:24.493
partly effective in noise.

00:06:24.974 --> 00:06:27.693
They help a great deal, without restoring normal

00:06:27.774 --> 00:06:28.413
hearing.

00:06:29.634 --> 00:06:32.193
The classic mistake is reading an average as

00:06:32.274 --> 00:06:34.993
if every patient improved that much.

00:06:35.074 --> 00:06:37.393
An average of seventy could hide some people

00:06:37.474 --> 00:06:40.833
near ninety and others who gained very little.

00:06:40.954 --> 00:06:43.713
Say what the average shows, then note the

00:06:43.794 --> 00:06:45.073
spread it hides.

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.340
So for any evaluate question, use the same

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.500
four moves.

00:06:50.780 --> 00:06:53.380
Say how the method or technology works.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.980
Judge what the evidence shows, with a fair

00:06:56.060 --> 00:06:56.780
comparison.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.060
Name a real limit.

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.980
Then commit to a judgement for that case.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.420
That brings Module 8, and Year 12 Biology,

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:06.460
to a close.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.020
When you revise, come back to these practice

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:09.740
questions.

00:07:10.967 --> 00:07:12.406
Here are the key notes.

00:07:12.647 --> 00:07:14.566
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:14.647 --> 00:07:15.446
to copy them.
